==Strategy==
These first ten stages are very straightforward. Use the startoff to your advantage by building up cash, then use strong Area Attackers and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] to keep Baron Seal in check.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*Meatshields: Obviously, given the high pushing power of Gauntlet stages, you're going to need meatshields. The best ones here are [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]].
*Talented [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: While not too helpful when Baron Seal is on the field, they help tremendously for building money up at the beginning of the stage. Be careful not to underestimate your Can Can's strength, as it's possible for you to have your Can Can prematurely hit the base.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]: A strong Area Attacker who works to take care of the Shadow Boxer Ks and Gory Darks. He can also deal decent damage against the Zombie peons.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: Housewife Cat is an excellent unit here, being able to apply Slow against the Zories and Zang Roos, as well as being able to hit Baron Seal itself.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: The enemies in these stages are all powerful pushers with high DPS and great speed, so naturally Stone does a great job of keeping them still.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Cyberpunk is a very effective crowd-controller for this stage, since he has an effective ability and has good uptime.
*[[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]]: Chief is a very strong unit here, being able to deal huge damage to the Zombie enemies as well as clean up corpses.
*[[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]]: Urs' Colossus Slayer ability allows her to rack up huge DPS against Baron Seal as well as the supporting peons.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Disposable damage to either remove a peon, deal damage against a pushing threat, or even as supporting damage for Baron Seal.
*Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]]: A boosted LKD works great at supplying damage against Baron Seal. Also has an Attack combo with [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]], who works as a meatshield.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]]: Chronos' Freeze ability is extremely powerful here, especially in combination with Cyberpunk.
*[[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Shining Amaterasu]]: Every enemy in these stages have a trait, allowing Amaterasu to deal massive amounts of damage to them all at her safe 455 range. If you give her the Zombie Killer talent, she can also keep Zang Roos and Zories down for good.
*Anti-Red Ubers: Anti-Red Ubers have a chance to connect onto Baron Seal and potentialy speed up the stage. These not only include nukers like [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai DX]] and [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Thundia β]], but anti-Red CC like [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]] and [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]].
*Colossus Slayer Ubers: Obviously, any Uber with Colossal Slayer gains much higher damage against Baron Seal, helping speed up these stages. In particular, [[Sea Serpent Daliasan (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Daliasan]], [[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Sunrise Sirius]], [[Spectral Goth Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Lady of Deception Vega]], [[Terun (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Terun ζ]], [[Lightmother Aset (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Aset]] (specifically in true form), and [[Cat Tengu (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Master Tengu]] are very strong here.
*Many [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] with the inclusion of a few [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] units, like [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli the Bane]] and [[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Doom Phono]]: Since all of the enemies here are traited, you can find great use for just about every UBERFEST exclusive here, with the only exception being [[Baby Garu (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Aegis Garu]] and [[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]] due to the extremely aggressive nature of the stage.
*[[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]: With his Colossus Slayer Talent, Cosmo not only does crazy damage to Baron Seal, but can cripple the supporting threats. Cosmo's Wave Attack also comboes with his initial hit, which will cause the Zombie threats to take damage and not burrow.

